<title>GREECE: EIB, GREECE TO SIGN FIRST TRANCHE OF HIGHWAY LOAN.</title>
<headline>EIB, GREECE TO SIGN FIRST TRANCHE OF HIGHWAY LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece and the European Investment Bank (EIB) will sign on December 16 a loan agreement worth 45 billion drachmas, the first tranche of a loan for building the Elefsina-Stavros highway, the EIB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agreement will be signed by National Economy Minister Yannos Papantoniou and the EIB's vice-president, it said.</p>
<p>The EIB, the European Union's financing institution, has approved a total of 265 billion drachmas for the completion of the project. -Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
